# Build outputs. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and then compiles inside the
# image, so without this it copies Windows-built bin/ and obj/ into a Linux
# build. That is how a stale artifact survives a rebuild and produces a green
# result that does not correspond to the source.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.vs/
.idea/
**/.vscode/

# Local developer state, never part of an image.
**/*.user
**/secrets.json

# NOT ignored, and load-bearing: scripts/base-schema.v2.sql is pulled in as an
# EmbeddedResource by VibeSQL.Core.csproj. If it stops reaching the build
# context the resource lookup fails at runtime, not at compile time.
